The fix for crbug 576850257 (restricted: "Snapshot image resource sets before
iterating in ResourceFetcher"): chromium/src main commit
cdaf43b7de96e148efc31ab0c013c830ee8a2bd7 (main@{#1743865}), merged to the 159
branch as b23289faa2. Its 158 merge (Gerrit 8820327) is pending, as of
8127@{#1855}.

ResourceFetcher::UpdateImagePrioritiesAndSpeculativeDecodes() and
ReloadImagesIfNotDeferred() iterated over not_loaded_image_resources_ and
speculative_decode_candidate_images_ directly, while updating resource info or
starting loads can synchronously request new image resources and modify those
sets mid-iteration: a use-after-free in the renderer, reachable from a page.
The fix copies the sets into local HeapVectors before iterating.

This is the main commit's change without its test (resource_fetcher_test.cc),
regenerated against 158's file (the same at the .37 tag and at #1855; the main
commit's hunks apply to it at offsets only, with no fuzz). The result is
byte-identical to the file of the pending 158 merge's current patchset. Drop
this once 158 gets the fix (check that the merged change is the same).

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_fetcher.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_fetcher.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_fetcher.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_fetcher.cc
@@ -2342,12 +2342,16 @@
 }
 
 void ResourceFetcher::ReloadImagesIfNotDeferred() {
-  for (Resource* resource : not_loaded_image_resources_) {
+  // Copy to a vector so that the iteration stays valid even if `StartLoad()`
+  // re-entrantly modifies `not_loaded_image_resources_`.
+  HeapVector<Member<Resource>> not_loaded_snapshot(not_loaded_image_resources_);
+  for (Resource* resource : not_loaded_snapshot) {
     DCHECK_EQ(resource->GetType(), ResourceType::kImage);
     if (resource->StillNeedsLoad() && !ShouldDeferImageLoad(resource->Url())) {
       StartLoad(resource);
     }
   }
+  not_loaded_snapshot.clear();
 }
 
